  "legacyHoldReasons": {
    "f_7ucixw3thbngg": "DBIA318(p.58) treats Kannada baṭṭe, Kodagu batte, Tulu baṭṭe, Telugu baṭṭa and Kota bat as loans ultimately from Sanskrit paṭṭa cloth, explicitly rejecting derivation from vastra. The selected survey forms need an immediate-donor/transmission analysis; do not label them inherited or automatically jump to Sanskrit. Compound/paired responses also require constituent analysis.",
    "f_hya6k2gvaurcu": "Irula census pətənālɯ is glossed sixteen, but its final nālɯ resembles four, suggesting a fourteen-type formation. Do not relabel the response or assign ten+six without checking the original alignment/transcription.",
    "f_u27wzyvzzqc6u": "The full DEDR appendix57 places Tamil/Malayalam vāl, Kannada bāla, Kota vālm, Kodagu bālï and Telugu vālamu alongside CDIAL11572 vāla-/vāra-. The existing appendix parent f_wqel4vcg76coc has an empty Form label. Do not attach these survey responses to an unnamed parent or skip to a remote Sanskrit ancestor before the historical route and immediate donor/parent are resolved.",
    "f_xsqulxmbluwo2": "DEDR5496(a) explicitly gives veḷḷi star/Venus/silver and Kodagu boḷḷi mīnï morning star. These simple veḷḷi/beḷḷi or white/silver + star responses need that subsection, but the current parent is labelled veṇ-ṇey butter from subsection (b). Hold until the parent scope is repaired; do not attach a star or its white component to the butter head.",
    "f_y35hiffpjyi4y": "DEDR3013 explicitly questions derivation of Tamil/Malayalam taṅkam pure gold from Sanskrit ṭaṅka stamped gold coin. Survey taṅkam variants are not treated as securely inherited; ultimate origin and immediate contact route require resolution.",
    "f_p2snbr7u7xm3k": "Survey morning responses rāve/ravila/iravile resemble the night family, but DEDR2552 attests night rather than morning. The dawn/morning semantic transition or elicitation scope must be verified before linking."
  }
